refused: d348_locking_inside_a_locked_block.cy:8:9, line 8 column 9
 8 |         @concur::locked $b as $y:
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 what: this locks inside a locked block
 why:  a deadlock needs a task holding one lock while waiting for another, so locking inside a locked block is refused, and one block takes every lock it needs (D348, D349)
